%% Sangati AI — Escalation & Overload Flow
%% Mermaid sequence diagram: Full escalation path from initial alert to broadcast

sequenceDiagram
    participant R as Rules Engine
    participant S1 as Server (Tier 1)
    participant S2 as Captain (Tier 2)
    participant S3 as Manager (Tier 3)
    participant BC as Broadcast (Tier 4)
    participant LOG as Event Log

    Note over R,LOG: Alert: "Zone B dirty 5 min"

    R->>S1: Push alert to zone server<br/>Severity: HIGH<br/>Timer: 90s
    R->>LOG: alert_created {tier:1, recipient:server}

    Note over S1: ⏱ 90 seconds pass — no response

    R->>R: Escalation timer fires
    R->>S2: Push to captain<br/>"⬆ Zone B dirty 5 min<br/>Server did not respond (90s)"
    R->>LOG: alert_escalated {tier:2, recipient:captain}

    Note over S2: ⏱ 120 seconds pass — no response

    R->>R: Escalation timer fires
    R->>S3: Push to manager<br/>"⬆⬆ Zone B dirty 7 min<br/>Server + Captain no response"
    R->>LOG: alert_escalated {tier:3, recipient:manager}

    alt Manager acknowledges
        S3->>R: ACK
        R->>LOG: alert_ack {tier:3, by:manager}
        Note over R: Escalation chain stopped
    else Manager does not respond (180s)
        R->>R: Final escalation timer fires
        R->>BC: 🔴 BROADCAST to ALL devices<br/>"UNATTENDED: Zone B dirty 10+ min<br/>No response from any staff"
        R->>LOG: alert_broadcast {tier:4}
    end

    Note over R,LOG: Simultaneous Overload Scenario

    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over R: Multiple zones degrading simultaneously
        R->>S3: "Zone A: idle 10 min" (escalated)
        R->>S3: "Zone B: dirty 6 min" (escalated)
        R->>S3: "Entry: queue 8 min" (escalated)
        R->>R: Fatigue check: manager at 3/5 limit

        Note over S3: Manager overwhelmed
        S3->>R: Switches to QUIET mode
        R->>R: Suppress non-critical alerts
        R->>LOG: mode_change {from:FULL, to:QUIET}
    end
